window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-082.json",{"day":82,"title":"A Market for Things with Another Life","targetWords":[{"word":"staple","gloss":"订书钉","context":"A staple secured an instruction sheet to an envelope, and a colored dot indicated that an item had passed a safety check.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"string","gloss":"线","context":"Learners practiced tying a knot with string before handling a delicate strand of fabric.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"wardrobe","gloss":"衣柜","context":"An antique wardrobe had a sticking drawer; a sofa needed a cushion; a couch had lost one bolt.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"badge","gloss":"徽章","context":"Every volunteer wore a badge, but no expensive outfit was required.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"banquet","gloss":"宴会","context":"They also asked whether describing the event as a recycling banquet sounded insensitive to residents living near a slum.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"bundle","gloss":"一捆","context":"The neighborhood market began with a bundle of unwanted cloth and a postcard announcing a repair day.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"cloth","gloss":"布","context":"The neighborhood market began with a bundle of unwanted cloth and a postcard announcing a repair day.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"dot","gloss":"圆点","context":"A staple secured an instruction sheet to an envelope, and a colored dot indicated that an item had passed a safety check.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"envelope","gloss":"信封","context":"A staple secured an instruction sheet to an envelope, and a colored dot indicated that an item had passed a safety check.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"knot","gloss":"结","context":"Learners practiced tying a knot with string before handling a delicate strand of fabric.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"purse","gloss":"钱包","context":"A broken umbrella required a new strap, a briefcase needed stitching, and a purse had a damaged fastening.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"soap","gloss":"肥皂","context":"The team used soap and a rag before deciding whether anything was beyond repair.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"tile","gloss":"瓷砖","context":"A volunteer found that a little glue could secure a loose tile, while a scrap of wood could replace a missing shelf.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"umbrella","gloss":"伞","context":"A broken umbrella required a new strap, a briefcase needed stitching, and a purse had a damaged fastening.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"antique","gloss":"古旧的","context":"An antique wardrobe had a sticking drawer; a sofa needed a cushion; a couch had lost one bolt.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"basement","gloss":"地下室","context":"A basement collection supplied the first donations.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"blanket","gloss":"毯子","context":"A worn blanket became a cozy rug for the reading corner, and a sack held cleaning materials.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"couch","gloss":"长沙发","context":"An antique wardrobe had a sticking drawer; a sofa needed a cushion; a couch had lost one bolt.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"cozy","gloss":"舒适的","context":"A worn blanket became a cozy rug for the reading corner, and a sack held cleaning materials.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"cushion","gloss":"靠垫","context":"An antique wardrobe had a sticking drawer; a sofa needed a cushion; a couch had lost one bolt.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"drawer","gloss":"抽屉","context":"An antique wardrobe had a sticking drawer; a sofa needed a cushion; a couch had lost one bolt.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"glue","gloss":"胶水","context":"A volunteer found that a little glue could secure a loose tile, while a scrap of wood could replace a missing shelf.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"rug","gloss":"地毯","context":"A worn blanket became a cozy rug for the reading corner, and a sack held cleaning materials.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"sack","gloss":"袋子","context":"A worn blanket became a cozy rug for the reading corner, and a sack held cleaning materials.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"scrap","gloss":"废料","context":"A volunteer found that a little glue could secure a loose tile, while a scrap of wood could replace a missing shelf.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"stall","gloss":"货摊","context":"They set up a stall beside the community canteen and hung a banner explaining the rules.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"strand","gloss":"线股","context":"Learners practiced tying a knot with string before handling a delicate strand of fabric.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"banner","gloss":"横幅","context":"They set up a stall beside the community canteen and hung a banner explaining the rules.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"bin","gloss":"垃圾箱","context":"Organizers hoped to prevent useful objects from entering a bin simply because their owners no longer needed them.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"bolt","gloss":"螺栓","context":"An antique wardrobe had a sticking drawer; a sofa needed a cushion; a couch had lost one bolt.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"canteen","gloss":"食堂","context":"They set up a stall beside the community canteen and hung a banner explaining the rules.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"fence","gloss":"栅栏","context":"By closing time, volunteers had repaired a fence panel, reunited a fork with a donated dining set, and taught children why they should bathe a dusty toy carefully rather than throw it away.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"fork","gloss":"叉","context":"By closing time, volunteers had repaired a fence panel, reunited a fork with a donated dining set, and taught children why they should bathe a dusty toy carefully rather than throw it away.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"furnace","gloss":"炉子","context":"A damaged furnace needed a qualified technician, and a hotel suite renovation had produced electrical equipment whose condition was unknown.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"outfit","gloss":"服装","context":"Every volunteer wore a badge, but no expensive outfit was required.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"postcard","gloss":"明信片","context":"The neighborhood market began with a bundle of unwanted cloth and a postcard announcing a repair day.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"rag","gloss":"破布","context":"The team used soap and a rag before deciding whether anything was beyond repair.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"rein","gloss":"马缰","context":"Someone donated an old riding rein, which became a carrying handle.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"sofa","gloss":"沙发","context":"An antique wardrobe had a sticking drawer; a sofa needed a cushion; a couch had lost one bolt.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"vacuum","gloss":"吸尘器","context":"A vacuum removed years of dust, making neglected objects look useful again without disguising their age.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"bathe","gloss":"清洗","context":"By closing time, volunteers had repaired a fence panel, reunited a fork with a donated dining set, and taught children why they should bathe a dusty toy carefully rather than throw it away.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"booth","gloss":"小隔间","context":"A bench offered rest for older visitors, while a booth provided quiet advice.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"briefcase","gloss":"公文包","context":"A broken umbrella required a new strap, a briefcase needed stitching, and a purse had a damaged fastening.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"slot","gloss":"专门时段","context":"The organizers set aside a slot for professional assessment rather than selling it immediately.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"slum","gloss":"贫民窟","context":"They also asked whether describing the event as a recycling banquet sounded insensitive to residents living near a slum.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"strap","gloss":"带子","context":"A broken umbrella required a new strap, a briefcase needed stitching, and a purse had a damaged fastening.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"suite","gloss":"套房","context":"A damaged furnace needed a qualified technician, and a hotel suite renovation had produced electrical equipment whose condition was unknown.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"torch","gloss":"手电筒","context":"A local historian displayed an artifact illustrating earlier reuse practices, while a borrowed torch illuminated its details.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"artifact","gloss":"旧物","context":"A local historian displayed an artifact illustrating earlier reuse practices, while a borrowed torch illuminated its details.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"bench","gloss":"长凳","context":"A bench offered rest for older visitors, while a booth provided quiet advice.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"The neighborhood market began with a bundle of unwanted cloth and a postcard announcing a repair day. Organizers hoped to prevent useful objects from entering a bin simply because their owners no longer needed them. They set up a stall beside the community canteen and hung a banner explaining the rules. Every volunteer wore a badge, but no expensive outfit was required. A bench offered rest for older visitors, while a booth provided quiet advice. The central idea was straightforward: value should not disappear at the moment an object changed hands.","zh":"社区市场起于一捆闲置布料和一张宣传维修日的明信片。组织者希望有用物品不要仅因主人不再需要就被扔进垃圾桶。他们在社区食堂旁设摊，挂上说明规则的横幅。志愿者佩戴徽章，不需要昂贵服装。长椅供老年访客休息，小隔间提供安静咨询。核心想法很简单：物品换主人时，其价值不应随之消失。"},{"en":"A basement collection supplied the first donations. An antique wardrobe had a sticking drawer; a sofa needed a cushion; a couch had lost one bolt. A volunteer found that a little glue could secure a loose tile, while a scrap of wood could replace a missing shelf. A worn blanket became a cozy rug for the reading corner, and a sack held cleaning materials. The team used soap and a rag before deciding whether anything was beyond repair. A vacuum removed years of dust, making neglected objects look useful again without disguising their age.","zh":"地下室的积存物品提供了第一批捐赠。古旧衣柜的抽屉卡住，沙发需要靠垫，另一张长沙发少了一颗螺栓。志愿者发现，一点胶可以固定松动瓷砖，废木料可以补上缺失架板。旧毯子变成阅读角的舒适地毯，袋子装着清洁用品。团队先用肥皂和抹布清理，再判断物品是否无法修复。吸尘器除去多年灰尘，让被忽视的物品重新显得有用，却没有掩饰其年代。"},{"en":"The busiest area concerned small repairs. A broken umbrella required a new strap, a briefcase needed stitching, and a purse had a damaged fastening. Learners practiced tying a knot with string before handling a delicate strand of fabric. A staple secured an instruction sheet to an envelope, and a colored dot indicated that an item had passed a safety check. Someone donated an old riding rein, which became a carrying handle. Such changes were modest, but they showed how attention to a weak connection could extend an object's life far more cheaply than complete replacement.","zh":"最忙碌的区域处理小修理。破伞需要新带子，公文包需要缝补，零钱包的扣件坏了。学习者先用细绳练习打结，再处理纤细织物线股。订书钉把说明纸固定到信封，彩色圆点表示物品通过安全检查。有人捐来旧马缰，改成提手。这些改变很小，却表明关注薄弱连接，可以比整体更换便宜得多地延长物品寿命。"},{"en":"Not everything belonged on the trading tables. A damaged furnace needed a qualified technician, and a hotel suite renovation had produced electrical equipment whose condition was unknown. The organizers set aside a slot for professional assessment rather than selling it immediately. They also asked whether describing the event as a recycling banquet sounded insensitive to residents living near a slum. A local historian displayed an artifact illustrating earlier reuse practices, while a borrowed torch illuminated its details. The discussion reminded everyone that environmental enthusiasm should not turn hardship into a fashionable spectacle.","zh":"不是所有东西都适合放上交易桌。损坏的炉子需要合格技师，酒店套房翻修产生的电器状态不明。组织者安排专门时段供专业评估，而非立即出售。大家也讨论，把活动描述成回收盛宴，是否会让贫困社区附近的居民感到不被体谅。地方历史研究者展示了一件反映过去重复利用方式的旧物，借来的手电筒照亮细节。讨论提醒大家，环保热情不该把困境变成时髦表演。"},{"en":"By closing time, volunteers had repaired a fence panel, reunited a fork with a donated dining set, and taught children why they should bathe a dusty toy carefully rather than throw it away. More important, they had created relationships around practical knowledge. People returned the following week to explain whether a repair had lasted, and those reports improved the next attempt. The market was not a universal answer to waste. It was a useful local institution in which repair became visible, ordinary, and open to people who had never considered themselves technically skilled.","zh":"收摊时，志愿者修好了围栏板，把一把叉子配回捐来的餐具，并教孩子为何应仔细洗净积灰玩具，而不是扔掉。更重要的是，大家围绕实用知识建立了关系。下一周，人们回来说明维修是否耐用，这些反馈改善了后续尝试。市场并非解决浪费的万能答案，而是实用的地方机构，让维修变得可见、平常，并向从未认为自己具备技术的人开放。"}],"previous":81,"next":83});
